22343.sol:
Let $\mathbf{a}=3 \mathbf{i}+\mathbf{j}+2 \mathbf{k}$ and $\mathbf{b}=\mathbf{i}+\mathbf{j}+2 \mathbf{k} \begin{gathered}
\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}=\left|\begin{array}{lll}
\mathbf{i}$& $\mathbf{j}$ & $\mathbf{k}$ \\
3 & 1 & 2 \\
1 & 1 & 2
\end{array}\right| \\
=\mathfrak{i}(2-2)-\mathfrak{j}(6-2)+$\mathbb{k}(3-1)=-4 \mathfrak{j}+2 \mathbf{k}
\end{gathered} |\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}|=\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(2)^{2}}=\sqrt{16+4}=\sqrt{20}$ Since, $|\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}|=|\mathbf{a}||\mathbf{b}| \sin \theta$,
If $\theta$ is angle between $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$. $\begin{aligned} \sqrt{20}$&=$\sqrt{9+1+4} \sqrt{1+1+4} \sin \theta$\\
\Rightarrow \sin $\theta$&=$\frac{\sqrt{20}}{\sqrt{6} \sqrt{14}}$\\
\Rightarrow \sin $\theta$&=$\sqrt{\frac{20}{6 \times 14}}=\sqrt{\frac{5}{21}}
\end{aligned}$

